    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0300" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d154-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Excerpt]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-12-16">16 December 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>853. I thank you cordially for your telegram Number 674 about Poland. I trust you
                    will carry out your proposal to send a message to Stalin suggesting that he
                    postpone any positive action on the Polish <pb facs="0301" n="217"
                        xml:id="pg217"/> question until the three of us can get together. This
                    suggestion is most valuable and also I feel extremely urgent. Would it be
                    possible for you to do this today, as I apprehend Stalin may make some move
                    recognizing the Lublin Committee as the government of Poland.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Prime</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
